{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 31","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular octagon is to be formed by cutting equal isosceles right triangles from the corners of a square. \nIf the square has sides of one unit, the leg of each of the triangles has length: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/26674cea4203dca019f53e7945ac3cf773744a3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"600\" height=\"41\" />   \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e3683cda4f3d70ffd3c8ba09e07b22d4c27955cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  real x = 8*(2-sqrt(2))/2;  // Square draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,8)--(0,8)--(0,0));  // Corners draw((0,x)--(x,0)); draw((8-x,0)--(8,x)); draw((8,8-x)--(8-x,8)); draw((x,8)--(0,8-x));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let the side length of the regular octagon be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and let the length of the legs of the isosceles right triangles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. The triangles are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=45-45-90&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"45-45-90 (page does not exist)\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22231a5cdd4fe05a11f4b577e3b81221f3017a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45-45-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /></a> triangles, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295c92e0ae9c0dec8ebf4971d1c1217c600d1be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=x\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"21\" />. Because each side of the square is length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and is composed of two legs of the triangles and one side of the octagon, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/a/c3af4be906c98ef2e3b9795ed110aafaee2d93c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+s=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295c92e0ae9c0dec8ebf4971d1c1217c600d1be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=x\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"21\" /> into this equation, we can now solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to get our desired answer:\n\\begin{align*}\n2x+s &amp;= 1 \\\\\n2x+x\\sqrt2 &amp;= 1 \\\\\nx(2+\\sqrt2) &amp;= 1 \\\\\nx &amp;= \\frac{1}{2+\\sqrt2} \\cdot \\frac{2-\\sqrt2}{2-\\sqrt2} \\\\\nx &amp;= \\frac{2-\\sqrt2}{4-2} = \\frac{2-\\sqrt2}{2}\n\\end{align*}\nThus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793d98aecdec018b7cfdd9f05ccedcc4d6cbdde3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"107\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1957 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1957\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">Problem 32</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wik